.TH TOSTEP 1
.SH NAME
tostep \- write solids as STEP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tostep
.IR stream.st | \-
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Tostep
writes each part of a stream
.RI ( stream (5)),
a folded blank or an exact solid, as a manifold solid of one STEP file
on the standard output, in world mm, a solid for each shell.
A part with a material is given an AP214 surface style in its color.
.PP
It may be the last program of a pipe.
Source lines left unused by the pipe, and void shells, are refused.
Faces are planes, cylinders, cones, spheres and tori, and pipes, the
rounds along ellipses, which no STEP surface of its own is: each is
written as a rational B-spline surface of degree 6 by 2 that is the
pipe, exactly, over the face and some room round it.
Ellipses, and arcs of circles on spheres and on pipes, are written as
several edges on one curve.
A nodal section of a torus
.RI ( stream (5)),
which no STEP curve is, is written as edges on cubic B-splines, which
meet it and its tangents at their ends and keep within about 1e-10 mm
of it; its faces stay exact.
.SH SEE ALSO
stream(5), part(5), smfold(1), tomesh(1)
